Kubernetes term        	Simple meaning
Cluster                	Complete Kubernetes environment
Node                  	Machine/server where workloads run
Pod                  	Smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes
Container            	Application packaged with its dependencies
Deployment	           Manages multiple copies of Pods
Service	            Gives stable network access to Pods
Namespace             	Logical separation inside a cluster
ConfigMap	           Stores non-secret configuration
Secret	                Stores sensitive information
Ingress             	Routes external HTTP/HTTPS traffic



role.yaml               	Defines what permissions a user/service account has inside one namespace
rolebinding.yaml        	Connects a Role to a user/service account
clusterrole.yaml	        Defines permissions that can apply across the cluster
clusterrolebinding.yaml	  Connects a ClusterRole to a user/service account across the cluster


persistentvolume.yaml (PV)         	Actual storage available to Kubernetes
persistentvolumeclaim.yaml (PVC)	  Request for storage by an application
storageclass.yaml                  	Defines how storage should be dynamically created

hpa.yaml                Automatically increases/decreases the number of Pods based on resource usage
networkpolicy.yaml      Controls which Pods are allowed to communicate with other Pods
serviceaccount.yaml     Creates an identity for a Pod/application to use when accessing Kubernetes resources


